{"hits": {"hits": [{"metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Collins, John C."}, {"full_name": "Wilczek, Frank"}, {"full_name": "Zee, A."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "18", "artid": "242", "year": 1978, "page_start": "242", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Collins:1978wz"], "abstracts": [{"value": "It is argued that in broken-symmetry theories the decoupling of heavy particles is incomplete. Some possible manifestations of this effect in neutral-current processes and the decay KL\u2192\u03bc\u03bc are discussed. In the case of the neutral current, heavy-particle effects may be calculated accurately including strong-interaction corrections. A new method of making such calculations is explained and its application to the neutral-current process discussed in detail. The method is more efficient than previous ones and is especially useful in calculations involving several mass scales."}], "control_number": 6481, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.18.242"}], "titles": [{"title": "Low-Energy Manifestations of Heavy Particles: Application to the Neutral Current"}], "author_count": 3, "document_type": ["article"]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6481?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6481?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6481?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6481?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6481?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6481?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A6481"}, "id": "6481", "created": "1978-04-01T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T03:34:31.618761+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C18%2C242&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprin